[agent] Done. The feature group `scaledaff2b3` (version 1) exists on the Hopsworks platform, online-enabled, with the correct standardized data.
[agent] **What was delivered**
[agent] - Feature group `scaledaff2b3` v1 in project `mlpabf9e24f`, primary key `row_id`, columns `row_id, split, f1, f2, f3, f4`, with the online store enabled for low-latency lookup.
[agent] - 650 rows total: 400 with `split="train"` and 250 with `split="serve"`. Each feature was standardized as `(x − train_mean) / train_pop_std` — mean and population std (ddof=0) computed over the training rows only and applied to both splits — then rounded to 6 decimals.
[agent] **How it ran (all platform-side)**
[agent] - Uploaded the two CSVs to HopsFS (`Resources/aff2b3/`) via `hops files upload`, then ran a Python job on the cluster (`hops job deploy … --run --wait`) that computed the train-only statistics, standardized both splits, and created/inserted the online-enabled feature group.
[agent] - A second on-cluster job verified the result through both platform read paths: the online store returns all 650 rows with the right schema, and the offline read confirms train-split mean ≈ 0 and population std ≈ 1 for every feature.
[agent] **Environment quirks worth reporting**
[agent] - The sandbox blocks direct sockets to the cluster's private IPs, and `NO_PROXY=10.0.0.0/8` made the CLI bypass the permitted local HTTP proxy. I routed REST traffic through the proxy by using `--host https://***REDACTED***.nip.io --no-verify` (wildcard-DNS hostname for the same IP).
[agent] - Data-plane protocols that can't tunnel over an HTTP proxy (HopsFS/HDFS writes, ArrowFlight, Trino) are unreachable from this machine, so local `hops fg insert`, `hops fg preview`, and `hops sql` fail here — that's why ingestion and verification were done via platform jobs. Also, the Hopsworks Query Service ArrowFlight endpoint initially returned "unavailable" even on-cluster on the first attempt, but succeeded on the retry.
